{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונאם הגבר", :translit "u-ne'um ha-gever", :gloss "and the utterance of the man"} {:he "קרא גבר", :translit "kara gever", :gloss "He called [him] gever"} {:he "כד\"א", :translit "ke-de Amar", :gloss "as that which is said"} {:he "שדומה בלעם לתרנגול", :translit "she-domeh bil'am la-tarnegol", :gloss "that Balaam is likened to a rooster"} {:he "כמו שהתרנגול הוא נואף מכל", :translit "ke-mo she-ha-tarnegol hu no'ef mi-kol", :gloss "just as the rooster is adulterous above all"} {:he "כן בלעם רבע אתונו", :translit "khen bil'am rav'a etono", :gloss "so Balaam copulated with his donkey"} {:he "כמו שהתרנגול יודע העתים", :translit "ke-mo she-ha-tarnegol yode'a ha-itim", :gloss "just as the rooster knows the hours"} {:he "כן בלעם ידע לכוון השעה שהקדוש ברוך הוא כועס בה", :translit "khen bil'am yada le-chaven ha-sha'ah she-ha-kadosh barukh hu ko'es bah", :gloss "so Balaam knew how to pinpoint the hour in which the Holy One blessed be He is angry in it"} {:he "כמו שהתרנגול דרכו לעמוד על רגל אחד", :translit "ke-mo she-ha-tarnegol darko la-amod al regel echad", :gloss "just as the rooster's way is to stand on one leg"} {:he "כן בלעם חגר באחת מרגליו", :translit "khen bil'am chagar be-achat mi-raglav", :gloss "so Balaam limped on one of his legs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: the word גבר in our verse triggers the association with the word גבר used elsewhere for a rooster."}], :frame {:text "The Sages identify three signs by which one can recognize practitioners of bestiality; one of them is that they limp on one leg (Sanhedrin 105a). The same passage records that Balaam was lame in one leg. The tradition that Balaam engaged in bestiality with his donkey derives from Sanhedrin 105a. The Talmud also states that Balaam knew how to identify the precise moment when God is angry and utters a curse in that instant (Sanhedrin 105b; Berakhot 7a). The term גבר itself carries connotations of strength or physical potency.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 105a" "Sanhedrin 105b" "Berakhot 7a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: the word גבר in our verse triggers the association with the word גבר used elsewhere for a rooster.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:07.996446985Z", :model "glm-5.2"}